/-!
# A Lean-checked run of THE target computing gcd(12, 18) (shard C)

**Problem, plainly.** Simulations say the decoded gcd_ps circuit computes gcd. Is there a behaviour that
provably satisfies every gate relation of THE theorem's circuit (`Behaves` at g = 1, κ = 0) and does
compute? **Proved** (`behaves_w1`, `w1_result`): the behaviour `xW1` (generated by
formal/tools/cview/witn1.py: power-up consistent with every gate under reset, operand buses at 12 and
18, reset released at 400 ns, the shared request raised at 401 ns and lowered once all three input
acknowledges are high, out0's and pend's acknowledges following their requests after 3 ns; every pin read
at its FAST_MIN; 97,926 transitions on 39,051 nodes) satisfies `Behaves p1 (circuit DecodedPS.net
DecodedPS.boundary)`, every gate kernel-checked at every breakpoint (`X*.lean`); in it out0's request
rises at 771,456 ps and its data bus reads `Nat.gcd 12 18 = 6` at 774,455 ps (3 ns after the request, the last ps before the acknowledge rises).
This is a single run, not a theorem about all runs; the Env/SeqEnv clauses for it are not proved here.
-/

